Package: speech-dispatcher-ru-normalizr
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-num2words (>= 0.5.13), python3-num2words (<< 0.6),
         python3-roman, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: speech-dispatcher-text-normalizer
Description: Russian text normalizer for the speech-dispatcher modules
 ru-normalizr turns numbers, dates, units and abbreviations of Russian text
 into words before a voice reads it. This package keeps it and the libraries
 Ubuntu lacks (pymorphy3 with its Russian dictionary, eng_to_ipa,
 phonenumbers) in a private directory for tts-normalize, outside the system
 Python. The modules use it only when speech-dispatcher-ru-normalizr-data is
 missing or with "TextNormalizationEngine python".

Package: speech-dispatcher-ru-normalizr-data
Section: text
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: data of the C Russian text normalizer for the speech-dispatcher modules
 The speech-dispatcher-modules voices normalize Russian text ("5 кг" ->
 "пять килограммов") with rn, a C port of ru-normalizr built into them. It
 needs the pymorphy3 Russian dictionary as one memory-mapped file
 (cmorphy3-ru.bin) and the CMU pronunciations of English words as eng_to_ipa
 gives them (en-ipa.tsv); both are made at build time from the libraries
 packaged in speech-dispatcher-ru-normalizr. No Python is needed at run time.
